"https://link.axios.com/img/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94as7f04.aaj1/263d346e.gif\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding-right:3.5%\" align=\"right\"> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLXBtLTljNjg1NmI4LTE4MjAtNDBjYy04YjRjLTUwYmQ4NzAxM2JjZi5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB885ede0d\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"b\" style=\"color:#222;font-size:13px;font-family:'gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-decoration:underline\">View in browser</a> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"30\" style=\"height:30px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1\">\r\n<span class=\"s\" style=\"font-size:44px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#008dc8;letter-spacing:-1px;line-height:1\"> Axios PM </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.5;padding-bottom:35px;padding-top:10px\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#222;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">By  Mike Allen  <span style=\"margin:0 6px\">&middot;</span> Sep 07, 2026 </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.75;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;padding:0 3.5%\"><p><strong>🇺🇸 Good Labor Day afternoon. </strong>Today's newsletter, edited by Alex Fitzpatrick, is 569 words, a 2-min. read. <em>Thanks to Sheryl Miller for copy editing</em>. </p><p>⚡️ <strong><em>Situational awareness: </em></strong><em></em>The U.S. is exploring whether Ukraine and Russia could take steps to de-escalate their war during the winter while restarting negotiations toward a broader peace agreement, <em>Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky tells Axios' Barak Ravid</em>. <em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMDkvMDcvemVsZW5za3ktdWtyYWluZS1ydXNzaWEtd2FyLXdpdGtvZmYta3VzaG5lci1wdXRpbi10cnVtcD91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc3BtJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB746da08e\" target=\"_blank\">Go deeper</a>.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing — Iran war&#x27;s energy bill: $100B and rising </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><div align=\"center\"><!--[if mso]><img alt='' src='https://images.axios.com/_VqHnfXZQu1oz1f-Ht2hwzYSsFI=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/07/14/1784052682617.jpeg' style='display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;' width='558' /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.axios.com/_VqHnfXZQu1oz1f-Ht2hwzYSsFI=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/07/14/1784052682617.jpeg\" style=\"display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;\" width=\"100%\"/><!--<![endif]--></div> <div class=\"bodytext\" style=\"font-size:13px; font-family:'Gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; color:#848484; margin-bottom:20px;\">Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images</div><p><strong>The war with Iran </strong>has now cost U.S. consumers $100 billion in higher energy prices, <em>Axios' Ben Berkowitz writes from a real-time Brown University estimate.</em></p><ul><li><strong>The bill is rising</strong> another $1 million about every two minutes.</li></ul><p><strong>🤑 By the numbers:</strong> The Iran War Energy Cost Tracker from Brown's Watson School says higher gasoline and diesel prices have cost the average U.S. household more than $760<strong> </strong>since the war began Feb. 28. <em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly9pcmFud2FyY29zdC53YXRzb24uYnJvd24uZWR1Lz91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc3BtJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBea03d51c\" target=\"_blank\">(Latest numbers.)</a></em></p><ul><li><strong>Most of that is gas, </strong>though the diesel burden is rising faster lately.</li></ul><p><strong>Stunning stat: </strong>The average national price of a gallon of regular gas was $4.15 today, <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly9nYXNwcmljZXMuYWFhLmNvbS8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NwbSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB63b5dee7\" target=\"_blank\">per AAA. </a></p><ul><li><strong>That's nearly a dollar</strong> higher than last year, and well above the previous Labor Day weekend record of $3.82 from 2012.</li></ul><p><strong>☢️ President Trump </strong>insists Americans are willing to pay higher prices to keep Iran from having a nuclear weapon. Yet voters consistently say inflation is the most important issue.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMDkvMDcvaXJhbi1nYXMtcHJpY2VzLWRpZXNlbC0xMDAtYmlsbGlvbj91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc3BtJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB59f75967\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Go deeper</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtcG0tOWM2ODU2YjgtMTgyMC00MGNj