\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-email-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Email this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-sms-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Text this Story\"></a></td></tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  2. ✈️ Investigators probe Amazon crash </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><div align=\"center\"><!--[if mso]><img alt='' src='https://images.axios.com/LWtmj044CwZnQsydxvSUsrkF94s=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/09/07/1788789140742.jpeg' style='display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;' width='558' /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.axios.com/LWtmj044CwZnQsydxvSUsrkF94s=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/09/07/1788789140742.jpeg\" style=\"display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;\" width=\"100%\"/><!--<![endif]--></div> <div class=\"bodytext\" style=\"font-size:13px; font-family:'Gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; color:#848484; margin-bottom:20px;\">An Amazon cargo plane after crashing at Miami International Airport yesterday. Photo: Joe Raedle/Getty Images</div><p><strong>Federal investigators are examining</strong> why an Amazon cargo jet barreled off a runway at Miami International Airport and into vehicles yesterday, killing at least five people.</p><ul><li><strong>They're likely to focus</strong> on whether the plane touched down too late to stop safely.</li></ul><p><strong>Video of the landing</strong> appears to show the Boeing 767 remaining airborne well down the runway before touching down. </p><ul><li><strong>Investigators will seek</strong> to determine exactly where the plane landed — and if it was beyond the normal touchdown zone, why the pilots did not abort the landing and circle back for another attempt.</li></ul><p><strong>Investigators will also examine</strong> the plane's speed and braking, weather and wind conditions, the aircraft's mechanical condition, and other factors.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly9hcG5ld3MuY29tL2FydGljbGUvY2FyZ28tcGxhbmUtY3Jhc2gtbWlhbWktYWlycG9ydC1hbWF6b24tcHJpbWUtZDUxMTg5OThlODgwZjM4MGEzZmQ4Nzg2ZTM1ZmQ5YmI_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NwbSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB49af98d6\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Get the latest</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtcG0tOWM2ODU2YjgtMTgyMC00MGNjLThiNGMtNTBiZDg3MDEzYmNmLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QyJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkyJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aC7d092348\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_dGV4dD0lRTIlOUMlODglRUYlQjglOEYlMjBJbnZlc3R