ine-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: ⚡️ Catch me up&body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20has%20shared%20an%20Axios%20story%20with%20you%3A%0A%0A⚡️ Catch me up%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2Fnewsletters%2Faxios-pm-9c6856b8-1820-40cc-8b4c-50bd87013bcf.html%3Fchunk%3D3%26utm_term%3Demshare%23story3\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-email-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Email this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-sms-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Text this Story\"></a></td></tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  4. 👽 1 science thing: The search for speck  </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><div align=\"center\"><!--[if mso]><img alt='' src='https://images.axios.com/2Z4sQZE3SASjduzGHW7kleyGE9E=/fit-in/1116x1300/2023/09/18/173941-1695058781206.jpg' style='display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;' width='558' /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.axios.com/2Z4sQZE3SASjduzGHW7kleyGE9E=/fit-in/1116x1300/2023/09/18/173941-1695058781206.jpg\" style=\"display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;\" width=\"100%\"/><!--<![endif]--></div> <div class=\"bodytext\" style=\"font-size:13px; font-family:'Gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; color:#848484; margin-bottom:20px;\">Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios</div><p><strong>In a new study, </strong>researchers propose searching for microscopic evidence of long-dead alien civilizations in lunar soil samples.</p><ul><li><strong>The idea is that</strong> tiny particles from collapsed civilizations could drift through space, perhaps settling on the Moon like flotsam and jetsam washing up on a beach.</li></ul><p><strong>📡 Ian Crawford,</strong> a professor of planetary science at<strong> </strong>Birkbeck College, University of London, and a study co-author, tells The New York Times: \"If you concede that looking for alien intelligences is a legitimate part of science ... then looking for the technological products ... ought to be just as scientifically valid as looking for their radio emissions.\"<em> (<a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.\" target=\"_blank\">Gift link</a>.)</em></p><p><strong>Reality check: </strong>The Moon is littered with microscopic junk from human spaceflight, and finding something alien in origin would be a long shot, to say the least.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly9hcnhpdi5vcmcvcGRmLzI2MDYuMjQwMjg_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NwbSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB5bd9fbd6\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Read the study</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtcG0tOWM2ODU2YjgtMTgyMC00MGNjLThiNGMtNTBiZDg3MDEzYmNmLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0Q0JTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3Rvcnk0JnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zcG0mc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aE43b31b35\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.480205/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: 👽 1 science thing: The search for speck &body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20has%20shared%20an%20Axios%20story%20with%20you%3A%0A%0A👽 1 science thing: The search for speck %0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2Fnewsletters%2Faxios-pm-9c6856b8-1820-40cc-8b4c-50bd87013bcf.html%3Fchunk%3D4%26utm_term%3Demshare%23story4\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-email-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Email this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47375284.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-sms-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Text this Story\"></a></td></tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size